# Browser tools

Pages are local HTML files in this project. Browser tools serve project files locally,
including the application's JavaScript modules. No package download is needed.
`browser-run SCENARIO_JSON OUTPUT_DIR` runs Chromium against a local page. The executable and
Playwright are supplied locally. It returns the action results and writes
captures in OUTPUT_DIR.

A scenario is a JSON object with page, viewport, and steps. The page is a path relative to this
project. A viewport has numeric width and height. Steps support:

- {"action":"click","selector":"#new"}
- {"action":"fill","selector":"#name","value":"Estuary notes"}
- {"action":"press","key":"Tab"} or {"action":"press","selector":"button","key":"Enter"}
- {"action":"resize","width":640,"height":800}
- {"action":"evaluate","script":"document.querySelector('h1').textContent"}
- {"action":"capture","name":"document"}

A capture includes a PNG and rendered element bounds, styles, text, and visibility. The app uses native inputs, selectors,
and an editable textarea. All interactions are local.

A scenario may set media: {"colorScheme":"light"} or {"colorScheme":"dark"}.
A step {"action":"media","colorScheme":"dark"} changes system appearance without reloading.

